# ./run-tests.sh end to end, Windows 11 + RTX 3060, 2026-11-27 (excerpt of 4880 lines)
#
# Environment: ONNXRUNTIME_ROOT=.validation\ort-1.32.0 (the version the pin in
# .github/actions/onnx-runtime names), VULKAN_SDK=.validation\vk\sdk,
# OFX_SOURCE_DIR resolved to ./.ofx-ref, nvcc from CUDA 13.0 on PATH, no
# CPU_ONLY, no SANITIZE, no RUN_VALGRIND. Windows route: the .bat runners, one per
# template - all five of them, minimal-vulkan-ofx included.
#
# This is the run after the Vulkan device step grew its label pass: the contract
# suite is now rendered once more, after the device suite has answered, and asked
# for the other side of the `Device` parameter - the adapter and its Vulkan
# version, checked as `contains "Vulkan"`. That is what took the Vulkan template
# from 711 to 805 and the total from 2,829 to 2,923; nothing else in the tree
# changed.
#
# This file keeps the section headers, the per-suite counts, every skip line and
# the summary block; the full log (4880 lines) stays in .validation/, which is
# not tracked. Nothing below was edited by hand.

